<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:36Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Taiwan: Home of semiconductor giants at the centre of AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56991c9b6a5111e965764a970e83d05ae2886382c8fcaa286b882255db885e70</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race--f4a0e175142c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race" /><summary type="html">The topic of artificial intelligence looms large as Chinese President Xi Jinping begins his highly anticipated state visit to Washington. The fate of Taiwan – coveted by its larger neighbour, China – will also be on the table. It's the global leader in superconductor research and development. These powerful chips can be found in smartphones, computers, and above all in AI development. Our France 2 colleagues take a rare look inside one of Taiwan's state-of-the-art laboratories.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Why is Trump rolling out the red carpet for China's Xi?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b2907dd81ab26dee9b4f40ac1ad5ef7b7622b5752fa0ac10d635495b4f773e5</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:11:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-why-is-trump-rolling-out-the-red-carpet-for-china-s-xi--fef5f241502f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-why-is-trump-rolling-out-the-red-carpet-for-china-s-xi" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump will host Chinese leader Xi Jinping at the White House on Thursday for a day full of pageantry. Trump personally greeted Xi on the tarmac after his arrival on Wednesday, the first time in more than six decades that a US president has welcomed a foreign political leader at Joint Base Andrews near Washington. But Trump's decision to roll out the red carpet has ruffled feathers among both Democrats and Republicans.</summary></entry><entry><title>Judge orders White House to restore access to barred media companies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e537d04546caa901fe4d6cf446c5749811bda0f4fd7cc4949843e96aaabe09f5</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-judge-orders-white-house-to-restore-access-to-barred-media-companies--60ea6c42aff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-judge-orders-white-house-to-restore-access-to-barred-media-companies" /><summary type="html">A federal judge temporarily blocked President Donald Trump’s ban of three news outlets from the White House grounds, ordering early Thursday that CNN, MS NOW and Politico must have their access restored.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tigrayan leaders say new war with Ethiopian govt has begun</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d613bd6901d794fe8c2456b524800f7de1dcb5ecd70cae487bac37e7e522e9b7</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:06:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-tigrayan-leaders-say-new-war-with-ethiopian-govt-has-begun--f3a85d0e1a5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-tigrayan-leaders-say-new-war-with-ethiopian-govt-has-begun" /><summary type="html">The TPLF says war has kicked off with the federal forces, four years after the end of the last conflict in Tigray which killed more than 600,000 people. The TPLF seized control of the airport in the capital of the northern region and fighting on the ground took place on the eastern border with Afar. It comes after months of tensions between Mekelle and Addis Ababa, and an announcement on Sunday of an alliance which aims to overthrow the prime minister. More from our correspondent Tom Canetti.)</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is paying for the pope’s visit to France?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b294ce4eef0a8c44ad040b1b5d1f489271c7de269faca858137acc7dbfd10c2</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:04:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-who-is-paying-for-the-pope-s-visit-to-france--a9f4020220fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-who-is-paying-for-the-pope-s-visit-to-france" /><summary type="html">Initially estimated at €12 million, the cost of Pope Leo XIV’s visit to France has now risen to €27 million due to the immense excitement around his trip. But with France a firmly secular country, who is going to be footing the bill? Our journalist Sam Ball explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mass shooting at a house party in South Africa kills 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ffa9e520d5709e64215c6b75853f4d0ce649b89ea881555dc9fdd40b8e41793</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:55:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-mass-shooting-at-a-house-party-in-south-africa-kills-11--a13332803ddf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-mass-shooting-at-a-house-party-in-south-africa-kills-11" /><summary type="html">Three gunmen barged into a small house in an impoverished neighborhood in South Africa and opened fire on a group enjoying a party inside, killing at least 11 people, police and local authorities said Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Does the future belong to China?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d7b0c7715f44ce56e81c4ba7e1068ccb6bf9d4d17f7dc2040632374f30e4676</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:32:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china--300d0d1807be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump is rolling out the red carpet for his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping ahead of Thursday's summit in Washington. But is China's leader overconfident in thinking the future belongs to Beijing? FRANCE 24's Yinka Oyetade speaks to Rex Li from King's College London.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>‘Massive, maximum destruction’: Putin seeks to bring Ukrainian civilians ‘to their knees’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13a23cd424d0e46126e9f82ea0ff53bb68fcaac00e1a986091d26b2001eccab3</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees--80c7cbe71ca4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev from Kyiv, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative. According to Zalmayev, Russia’s ongoing attacks on Ukraine reflect a broader political logic in which military force, political objectives and territorial ambitions are intertwined as instruments of Russian strategy. He argues that Moscow’s attacks on civilian infrastructure are designed to exert extreme pressure on Ukrainian society while demonstrating fierce retaliation to domestic audiences in Russia. Zalmayev contrasts this with Ukraine’s strikes on Russian energy infrastructure, which he describes as targeting assets that directly sustain Moscow’s war effort.</summary></entry><entry><title>Australia's Medicare AI hack: Its seriousness 'cannot be overstated'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ee1a75c70609d75105062227378c72c4c9f9973298d0b2308b28d1aab5088e7</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:11:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260924-australia-s-medicare-ai-hack-its-seriousness-cannot-be-overstated--ce6f4bf87a86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260924-australia-s-medicare-ai-hack-its-seriousness-cannot-be-overstated" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 24: The Spanish press express outrage after the forced eviction of an elderly woman from her Madrid residence. Unrest in the Tigray region sparks fears of a new war between rebels and Ethiopia's central government. Australian authorities reveal that the national health insurance system Medicare was hacked by an AI agent. Finally, we look at Britain's rudest-sounding street names!</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Huge security operation underway for Pope's visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a6412659c031733c9366a7ec0e8b50536ef9debab8a587286cbcf1b47fae678</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:09:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-huge-security-operation-underway-for-pope-s-visit-to-france--984a8089413c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-huge-security-operation-underway-for-pope-s-visit-to-france" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of the faithful and visitors are expected in Paris this weekend as Pope Leo XIV visits the French capital, marking the first papal visit to the country since 2008. France has pulled out all the stops to welcome the pontiff over the two-day visit in the capital and security forces are ensuring maximum protection with some 14,000 police officers, gendarmes, and soldiers mobilized across the capital.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's Tigray rebels in 'full-blown' war with govt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de065a493c5b202ba9184c6daeb14615bae762c0ef4aa3df645cbd46d6cd9449</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:38:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:05:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-in-full-blown-war-with-govt--583f86a1c75b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-in-full-blown-war-with-govt" /><summary type="html">Tigray rebels in Ethiopia told AFP on Thursday they were in a state of "full-blown war" with the federal government, as heavy artillery attacks were reported in neighbouring states. Tensions have been rising for months between the federal government and the authorities in the northern Tigray state, who fought a devastating civil war in 2020-2022 that killed more than 600,000 people, according to African Union estimates.</summary></entry><entry><title>Australia’s Albanese rebukes OpenAI after government website hacked</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e06f11ef5f1c499b7fffa10ed866252468164dcd250c56685b9744384891ae7b</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:02:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-australia-s-albanese-rebukes-openai-after-government-website-hacked--eb3384d39373.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-australia-s-albanese-rebukes-openai-after-government-website-hacked" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Anthony Albanese said Thursday he was extremely concerned about OpenAI 's breach of an Australian health department website and that the artificial intelligence company took too long to reveal the incident. An OpenAI agent infiltrated the public-facing Medicare Statistics Reporting Service portal on June 18, he said.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Particularly heavy night' of Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e723e5d293a6ec50d61a6f9a9397974dd6fa97ad42eae14df57c16a1a061ed9</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:59:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-particularly-heavy-night-of-russian-strikes-on-kyiv--0c84595ade14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-particularly-heavy-night-of-russian-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">France 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv where he says a "particularly heavy night" of Russian strikes on the Ukrainian capital involved the use of ballistic missiles.</summary></entry><entry><title>US says China trade truce extended as Trump welcomes Xi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57fefcc817d5d22945c64770d63d061dab30480a2f76fb2594a431b9e3e133cb</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-us-says-china-trade-truce-extended-as-trump-welcomes-xi--ed198b0003c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-us-says-china-trade-truce-extended-as-trump-welcomes-xi" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump welcomed Chinese President Xi ​Jinping to Washington on Wednesday for a three-day visit that will test relations between the superpowers as tensions simmer over trade, technology, Taiwan and Tehran. Xi’s first trip to the US in nearly three years was not expected to deliver major breakthroughs, but Washington and Beijing could extend their 11-month trade truce.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo in France: 'Huge amount of excitement building in Paris'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b52cddd5421f660c240ec4208f21eb132a7ca4501542080ce5c52b147efae717</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:54:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-pope-leo-in-france-huge-amount-of-excitement-building-in-paris--d6c54ec4fd1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-pope-leo-in-france-huge-amount-of-excitement-building-in-paris" /><summary type="html">France 24's Antonia Kerrigan reports from Paris as the French capital prepares for the arrival of Pope Leo XIV, where he is set to hold a huge open-air Mass.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelensky says Putin 'patient zero' for spreading war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36980c451a22404754b9235f379a9f75908c940af7c91dc23aaf89d674ec4cd7</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:11:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-ukraine-zelensky-says-putin-patient-zero-for-spreading-war--3d383f3c5c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-ukraine-zelensky-says-putin-patient-zero-for-spreading-war" /><summary type="html">🇺🇦 🇺🇳 Speaking at the UN General Assembly, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Russian President Vladimir Putin was "patient zero" for spreading war in the region with Moscow's invasion of Ukraine.
 
The Ukrainian president also asked world leaders to cut back on buying oil from Russia, in a bid to put pressure on Moscow to resolve the conflict swiftly.</summary></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump startled by the sound of a fighter jet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed2721f91ebd315c858815e9861525983f5173e492c1455dd7ad7c007889e3c6</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:03:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-startled-by-the-sound-of-a-fighter-jet--fd5a564dc607.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-startled-by-the-sound-of-a-fighter-jet" /><summary type="html">🇺🇸 🇨🇳 As Donald #Trump welcomed his Chinese counterpart Xi #Jinping for a state visit on the tarmac of an airport near #Washington, the sound of a fighter jet during the military ceremony caught the US president off guard, prompting a series of startled facial expressions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Discovery of ancient wall could confirm origins of Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c26210cc076e255823629c81cbd9d0e640ae0e32bb2e8cece84f2b261d978441</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T10:01:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-discovery-of-ancient-wall-could-confirm-origins-of-paris--c343478b649f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-discovery-of-ancient-wall-could-confirm-origins-of-paris" /><summary type="html">An ancient wall discovered in central Paris was hailed as a "major breakthrough" on Wednesday, as the archaeological find may have settled a long-standing debate about the location of the city's original settlement. A roughly 20-metre (66-foot) wall dating from the Gallo-Roman period was discovered in Paris this summer beneath a hospital on the Ile de la Cite, a stone's throw from Notre Dame Cathedral, the French culture ministry said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope's visit to France 'an important moment for the Vatican'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:178faf8792543d57e648d79b37317778676e3d66ec2eb450be6a5ad766e306c5</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T09:58:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-pope-s-visit-to-france-an-important-moment-for-the-vatican--0d5095998b30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-pope-s-visit-to-france-an-important-moment-for-the-vatican" /><summary type="html">France is gearing up for the arrival of Pope Leo XIV in what will be the first state visit to the country by a pontiff since 2008. Seema Gupta, France 24's correspondent in Rome takes a look at the visit from the Vatican's point of view.</summary></entry><entry><title>Fears of flooding, landslides as Hurricane Polo churns off Mexico coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5256fa048cd4590c973805f65010e7bfbe30e4dee7bc866b9936ecb18ed9d75d</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T09:53:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-fears-of-flooding-landslides-as-hurricane-polo-churns-off-mexico-coast--b0f139d7645e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-fears-of-flooding-landslides-as-hurricane-polo-churns-off-mexico-coast" /><summary type="html">Residents of Mexico's Pacific beach towns were preparing for heavy rain and dangerous surf ​on Wednesday ‌as Hurricane Polo, a powerful Category 4 storm, tracked northwestward just ⁠offshore, threatening flooding and mudslides along the country's southwestern coast.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘I felt like I'd been tricked’: France probes secret filming of women with smart glasses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0864e62b834d0e9545f23a4089288cb4d93e270ae86cf87edb5ac3dd537392c3</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T09:47:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-i-felt-like-i-d-been-tricked-france-probes-secret-filming-of-women-with-smart-glasses--fb2f5346b07a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-i-felt-like-i-d-been-tricked-france-probes-secret-filming-of-women-with-smart-glasses" /><summary type="html">It's a trend that first started in the US and is becoming more and more prevalent in France. Women are being filmed in the street without their knowledge, by men wearing smart glasses. The men are earning money by posting the videos online without the consent of their victims. Ellen Gainsford has details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump welcomes China's Xi to Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:440a9617e3dcfa761ecca7417bd33df22e509e5bb632ceaa314d5a6c6a54c2c5</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T09:46:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-trump-welcomes-china-s-xi-to-washington--f265faaffec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-trump-welcomes-china-s-xi-to-washington" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump welcomes Chinese President Xi Jinping to the White House on Thursday for a lavish state summit expected to be heavy on symbolism but light on substance, with both leaders keen to showcase stable ties despite a deep underlying rivalry. Trump greeted Xi on arrival on Wednesday evening, the first time a US president has welcomed a foreign leader at Joint Base Andrews in 11 years.</summary></entry><entry><title>A look back at Tunisia's summer of shortages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c1f3dbbaa1c47913cb2b0b5fc9610d1676acc71760d4f800670d75e33fa1410</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T09:43:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-look-back-tunisiassummer-shortages--1433d0807877.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-look-back-tunisiassummer-shortages" /><summary type="html">Repeated power and water outages, long queues for bottled water, and poultry farms destroyed by the heat: millions of Tunisians were affected by water and electricity shortages over the summer. Our Observers say this is the result of years of underinvestment. The water shortage eased in late August when authorities sent millions of bottles of water to stores, but many are concerned the same thing could happen next summer.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>'Risk to humanity': At UN, tech leaders urge caution in AI development</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0022f14137c619aaa60ef0e380dfb8332422050ff29ef914c5ad36391e32968</id><updated>2026-09-24T13:39:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T09:38:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-risk-to-humanity-at-un-tech-leaders-urge-caution-in-ai-development--3c8659312d02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-risk-to-humanity-at-un-tech-leaders-urge-caution-in-ai-development" /><summary type="html">The heads of major artificial intelligence firms pleaded with the United Nations on Wednesday to save the world or at least its people — by somehow regulating the fast-expanding technology that they have been designing. “If managed poorly, I even believe AI could be a risk to humanity as a whole,” said Dario Amodei, chief executive officer of Anthropic.</summary></entry></feed>
